 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 2,
   "text": "NORTH: Corwen, Llangollen and the Dee. Gogledd. Owain Glynd\u0175r was proclaimed Prince of Wales near here in 1400, and the Welsh have not entirely stopped cheering."
  },
  {
   "x": 5,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "WEST: Dolgellau, Machynlleth and the Cambrian Coast. Gorllewin. The road climbs, falls, and does it again, as if it were showing off."
  },
  {
   "x": 40,
   "y": 12,
   "text": "LLYN TEGID. Four miles long, a mile wide, and the largest natural lake in Wales. The River Dee runs through it from end to end, which is the sort of thing a lake does when it is determined to be useful."
  },
  {
   "x": 14,
   "y": 16,
   "text": "Y BALA. The name means the outlet, the place where a lake empties. The lake does not mind. It has been emptying here since the ice left."
  },
  {
   "x": 27,
   "y": 9,
   "plaque": "llyn_tegid_glyndwr",
   "title": "Glynd\u0175r's Proclamation",
   "text": "On 16 September 1400 Owain Glynd\u0175r was proclaimed Prince of Wales at his manor at Glyndyfrdwy, on the Dee between Llangollen and Corwen. The revolt that followed lasted over a decade. Glynd\u0175r was never captured and no one knows for certain where he died, which has kept the legend in good health."
  },
  {
   "x": 47,
   "y": 9,
   "plaque": "llyn_tegid_bible",
   "title": "Mary Jones and the Bible",
   "text": "In 1800 a Welsh girl of fifteen, Mary Jones, is said to have walked some twenty-five miles from her home to Bala to buy a Bible from the minister Thomas Charles. He had run out of copies. The story goes that he found her one anyway, and that her journey helped to inspire the founding of the British and Foreign Bible Society in 1804."
  },
  {
   "x": 54,
   "y": 22,
   "plaque": "llyn_tegid_gwyniad",
   "title": "The Gwyniad",
   "text": "The gwyniad is a whitefish that lives in Llyn Tegid and nowhere else in Wales, a relic of the cold water left behind when the glaciers melted. It is silver, shy and rare, and fishermen who catch one are asked politely to put it back."
  }
 ],
